N5008 [lex.string]/6: string literals are `const char[n]' lvalues, __func__ is
`static const char[]' ([dcl.fct.def.general]/8), sizeof of a reference type is
the size of the referenced type ([expr.sizeof]/2), and an array bound is
normalised to the index type so equal array types compare equal whichever way
the bound was spelled.  The legacy string-literal-to-`char *' conversion
(C++03 [conv.array]/2) is still accepted, ranked below every standard
conversion.
